<title>USA: Warm, high pressure returns for Brazil coffee -WSC.</title>
<headline>Warm, high pressure returns for Brazil coffee -WSC.</headline>
<dateline>LEXINGTON, Mass. 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Warm, high pressure aloft over Brazil is building back into the coffee belt and is expected to dominate the area for the coming week, Weather Services Corp said in an update on Thursday.</p>
<p>Mostly fair skies were observed in main growing areas of the belt this morning. Low temperatures were in the 50's F (10-15 C). Some cooler conditions were reported in higher elevations.</p>
<p>Fair skies are expected for the next seven days. Low temperatures will be in the 50's to low 60's F (low to middle teens C). Cooler conditions are still expected for higher elevations, although there is still no damaging cold indicated, according to WSC. ((--Eileen Houlihan, New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1640))</p>
